---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'HOA rules for parking an RV at home | RV Storage Finder';
const description =
  'Notes on homeowners’ association rules for an RV or boat kept at home. Florida is summarized from section 720.3045. Other states are not written up yet.';
const path = '/rules/';
const checked = '2026-11-19';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'HOA rules', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: checked }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>HOA rules for an RV or boat at home</h1>
    <p>
      These notes quote a statute and say what that sentence does not decide. They are not legal advice,
      and they are not a reading of your declaration, your city code, or a condominium document.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={href('/rules/florida/')}>Florida</a>. Section 720.3045, read on November 19, 2026.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Arizona, Texas, Georgia, Nevada, and North Carolina are not summarized here. A storage listing in
      those states is not a statement about driveway or HOA rules.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={href('/states/florida/')}>Florida storage listings</a> are off-site facilities, separate
      from parking on a parcel.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
